COMPLETE WEBHOOK INTEGRATION FIX: Successfully resolved 503 errors in YAYA dashboard chat interface by fixing service detection logic. Problem: Chat interface was getting 503 errors while webhook tests showed 200 success because system was using MockN8nService instead of real Railway n8n service. 

Solution: Updated shouldUseMockService() function in mock-n8n-service.ts to detect Railway URL:
```typescript
export function shouldUseMockService(): boolean {
  // Force use of real service when we have a Railway webhook URL configured
  if (process.env.N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL?.includes('primary-production-c041f.up.railway.app')) {
    return false
  }
  // Also check for the old n8n cloud URL for backwards compatibility  
  if (process.env.N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL?.includes('willem4130.app.n8n.cloud')) {
    return false
  }
  return !process.env.N8N_API_KEY || process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development'
}
```

Environment variables correctly set to:
- N8N_BASE_URL=https://primary-production-c041f.up.railway.app
- N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=https://primary-production-c041f.up.railway.app/webhook

Result: End-to-end webhook integration now fully functional - chat interface connects to real Railway n8n instance instead of mock service. Server restart required to pick up changes.
